hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6763","I ask You that when I enter Paradise, I am granted a white palace on the right side of Paradise."" So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O my son, ask Allah for Paradise and seek His protection from Hellfire. I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Soon there will come people in this Ummah who will exceed the limits in supplication and in purification.'"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration has been heard by Jariri from Yazid bin Abdullah and from Abu Na’ama, so both these chains are preserved."
"6764","Abdullah heard his son praying to Allah: O Allah, I ask Thee a white palace on the right of Paradise when I enter it. He said: O my son, ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge in Him from Hell-Fire, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: In this community there will be some people who will exceed the limits in purification as well as in supplication. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 96)"
"6765","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""In the last era, there will be some people who will belong to my Ummah; they will tell you things which neither you nor your forefathers have heard. So be cautious and beware of them."
"6766","I asked: Will this really happen? He replied: Yes, it will certainly happen."
"6767","The Hour will not be established (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) and among the signs of the Hour is that knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will become widespread, wine will be drunk, adultery will become common, and men will decrease while women will increase, to the extent that one man will be the guardian of fifty women.'"
"6768","""I shall narrate a Hadith to you that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which none after me shall narrate that he heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" [He said:] ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge shall be raised up, ignorance shall be rampant, Zina shall abound, Khamr shall be drunk, women shall increase and men shall decrease such that fifty women will be supported by one man."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2205)"
"6769","The Hour will not be established until there descends from the sky a rain from which no house made of clay will be saved, only houses made of hair will be saved."
"6770","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon the Muslims will be besieged in Madinah Munawwarah, to the extent that the farthest place to escape from their enemy will be 'Salaah' (which is near Khaybar)."
"6771","Ibn 'Umar reported the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: The Muslims will soon be besieged up to Medina, so that their most distant frontier outpost will be Salah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4250)"
"6772","Its inhabitants will abandon it, whereas it is good for them and it will become the haunt of beasts and birds. (Imam Muslim said that Abu Safwan, one of the narrators whose name was 'Abdullah b. 'Abd al-Malik, was an orphan and I bn juraij took him under his care for ten years.) (Using translation from Muslim 1389a)"
"6773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck that bunch with his staff and said: If the one giving charity had wished, he could have given better quality dates in charity. This person who gave charity will eat inferior quality dates on the Day of Resurrection. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards us and said: By Allah! O people of Madinah, you will leave (this Madinah) for the wild beasts. Do you know what is meant by 'Awafi'? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Birds and wild beasts (are meant)."
"6774","The Hour will not be established until Madinah expels its worst people in the same way that a furnace removes the impurities (i.e., rust) from iron."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also said: ""A time will come upon the people when a person will call his relative or his friend towards prosperity, although if those people knew, Madinah would be better for them."
"6775","The last settlement of the Muslims to be destroyed will be Madinah Munawwarah."
"6776","I will not remain among you for long, and you too will not remain for long after me. Soon you will face such a situation in which you will destroy one another, and before the Hour there will be two widespread severe deaths, and after that, for some years, earthquakes will continue to occur."
"6777","The narrator says: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described his appearance before us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is possible that someone may reach him who has seen me, or has heard my speech."" The people said: ""O Messenger of Allah! On that day, will our hearts be like they are today?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They will be even better than today."
"6778","I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: There has been no Prophet after Noah who has not warned his people about the antichrist (Dajjal), and I warn you of him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ described him to us, saying: Perhaps some who have seen me and heard my words will live till his time. The people asked: Messenger of Allah! what will be the condition of our hearts on that day? Like what we are today? He replied: Or better. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4756)"
"6779","I will tell you something about him which no prophet has told his nation. You should know that he is one-eyed, whereas your Lord is not one-eyed. Between his two eyes will be written 'Kafir' (disbeliever), which every believer will be able to read, whether he is literate or illiterate."
"6780","I am also warning you about him. He will surely appear among you."
"6781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He will not harm you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, people say that he will have rivers and food with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Despite all that, he will be the most insignificant in the sight of Allah Almighty."
"6782","No one asked Messenger of Allah ﷺ more about Dajjil than I asked him. He said: He should not be a source of worry to you for he would not be able to do any harm to you. I said: Messenger of Allah, it is alleged that he would have along with him (abundance of) food and water. Thereupon he said: He would be very insignificant in the eye of Allah (even) with all this. (Using translation from Muslim 2939a)"
"6783","We were walking with Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Ibn Sayyad happened to pass by him. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: I have concealed for you (something to test you, so tell me that). He said: It is Dukh. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Be off. You cannot get farther than your rank, whereupon 'Umar said: Messenger of Allah, permit me to strike his neck. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Leave him; if he is that one (Dajjal) whom you apprehend, you will not be able to kill him. (Using translation from Muslim 2924b)"
"6784","Do you bear testimony to the fact that I am the Messenger of Allah? Thereupon he said: Do you bear testimony to the fact that I am the messenger of Allah? Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I affirm my faith in Allah and in His Angels and in His Books, and what do you see? He said: I see the throne over water. Whereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You see the throne of Iblis upon the water, and what else do you see? He said: I see two truthfuls and a liar or two liars and one truthful. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Leave him He has been confounded. (Using translation from Muslim 2925)"
"6785","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may"
"6786","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit, praised and glorified Allah, and said: “I have not gathered you here out of desire or fear, but rather an incident has occurred which Tamim Dari has narrated to me. He says that he and thirty men from the tribes of Lakhm and Judham were traveling by sea. He narrated that the sea (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) the waves began to play with us, and this continued for a month, then our boat reached an island in the sea. Tamim Dari narrates: We disembarked and went towards the island, where we met a woman who was pulling at her hair. We could not tell whether she was coming or going. We asked: Who are you? She said: I am ‘Jassasah’. We said: Tell us something. She said: Go to the person in the church, he will inform you and will also ask you for information. Tamim Dari narrates: We went to him, and he was a man—then she mentioned his great size—he was bound with iron chains. We asked: Who are you? He said: First tell me about that which I will ask you. They said: Ask us. He asked: What is the condition of the date palms of Baisan? Are their fruits still being eaten? We replied: Yes. He said: Soon they will not be eaten. Then he asked: Tell me about the spring of Zughar, is there water in it? We replied: Yes. He said: Soon there will be no water in it. Then he said: Tell me about that man, has he appeared? They replied: Yes. He said: Indeed, he is truthful, so follow him. We asked: Who are you? He said: I am the Dajjal.” Kahmas narrates: Ibn Buraidah mentioned something here which I do not remember, but in it are these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The earth will be folded for him, so that he will circle the entire earth in forty days.”"
"6787","I am warning you about the Dajjal. Every prophet before me has warned his nation about him, and he will appear among you. O Ummah! Indeed, there is no prophet after me, and there is no nation after you. However, Tamim Dari has informed me that his cousin and his companions were traveling in the sea of Sham. They reached an island where there was a woman pulling her hair. They asked: Who are you? She said: Jassasah (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) Jassasah. They said: Tell us about something. She said: I will not tell you about anything, nor will I ask you about anything, but go to the place of worship, there is a man there who is eager to meet you. They went to the place of worship and found a man there, whose eye was defective, and he was bound in iron chains to a pillar. He asked: Where have you come from? Who are you? They replied: From the people of Sham. He asked: Who are you? They replied: We are Arabs. He said: What is the condition of the Arabs? They said: Among them, a prophet has appeared who is from the land of Tayma. He asked: What is the condition of the people? They said: Some of them have affirmed him, and some have denied him. He said: If they affirm him and follow him, it is better for them if they know. Then he asked: What are your houses made of? They said: Of hair and wool, which our women prepare. The narrator says: He struck his hand on his knees and said: That is it. Then he asked: What is the condition of the Lake of Tiberias? They said: Its shores are overflowing. He struck his hand on his knees and said: Hurry up. Then he asked: What is the condition of the spring of Zughar? They said: Its banks are overflowing, and whoever comes to it drinks to his fill. He struck his hand on his knees and said: Hurry up. Then he asked: What is the condition of the date palms of Baisan? They said: Their branches bear fruit all year round. He struck his hand on his knees and said: Hurry up. Then he said: If I am freed from these chains, there will be no spring that I will not trample, except for Makkah and Taybah (i.e., Madinah), for I am not permitted to go there. (The narrator says) Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is Taybah. I declare it sacred just as Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah sacred. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, on every path leading into it through the land and mountains, there are two angels stationed, with swords drawn, ready to prevent the Dajjal from entering it until the Day of Resurrection."
"6788","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came quic"
"6789","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Perform deeds before the appearance of six (signs): the Dajjal, the smoke, the Beast of the Earth, and the rising of the sun from the west.\"""""""
"6790","Hasten in performing these good deeds (before these) six things (happen): (the appearance) of the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast of the earth, the rising of the sun from the west, the general turmoil (leading to large-scale massacre) and death of masses and individuals. (Using translation from Muslim 2947b)"
"6791","The Dajjal will emerge from this direction""—the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) indicated towards the east (while saying this). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah's (may Allah be pleased with him) statement: ""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) indicated towards the east""—by this is meant Bahrain, because Bahrain is to the east of Madinah Munawwarah, and the emergence of the Dajjal will also be from these regions, not from Khurasan. The evidence for the correctness of this is: the Dajjal is tied up on an island in the sea, as Tamim Dari has informed regarding this, whereas in Khurasan there is neither a sea nor an island."
"6792","The seeing of Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and his striking was in the sense that Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) will also strike with a stick. This incident occurred during the blessed life of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6793","May Allah have mercy upon you, why did you incite Ibn Sayyad in spite of the fact that you knew it would be the extreme anger which would make Dajjal appear in the world? (Using translation from Muslim 2932a)"
"6794","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The eyes of the Dajjal will be green like glass. You should seek Allah's protection from the punishment of the grave.\"""""""
"6795","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: He will be one-eyed and very fair-skinned, his head will be small like a snake’s, and among the people, he will most resemble Abdul-Uzza bin Qatan. No matter how many people are destroyed, your Lord is not one-eyed."
"6796","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) replied: ""They will be few in number."
"6797","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: The people would run away from the Dajjal seeking shelter in the mountains. She said: Where would be the Arabs then in that day? He said: They would be small in number. (Using translation from Muslim 2945a)"
"6798","The Dajjal would be followed by seventy thousand Jews of Isfahan wearing Persian shawls. (Using translation from Muslim 2944)"
"6799","I know best what the Dajjal (Antichrist) will have with him. He will have with him a sea of water and a river of fire, and what you see as fire will be water and what you sea as water will be fire. If any of you who lives up to that time and desires water, he should drink from what he sees as fire, for he will find it water. Abu Mas’ud al-Badri said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in this way. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4315)"
"6800","I bear witness that you are the same Dajjal about whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us. So the Dajjal will say: What do you people think, if I kill him and then bring him back to life, will you have any doubt about this matter? The people will reply: No. So the Dajjal will be given power over this man; he will kill him and then bring him back to life. When he is brought back to life, he will say: By Allah! I have more insight about you now than I had before. Then the Dajjal will intend to kill this man again, but he will not be able to overpower him. The narrator named Mu'ammar says: People believe that the man whom the Dajjal will kill and then bring back to life is Sayyiduna Khidr (peace be upon him)."
"6801","He would come but would not be allowed to enter the mountain passes to Medina. So he will alight at some of the barren tracts near Medina, and a person who would be the best of men or one from amongst the best of men would say to him: I bear testimony to the fact that you are Dajjal about whom Messenger of Allah ﷺ had informed us. The Dajjal would say: What is your opinion if I kill this (person), then I bring him back to life; even then will you harbour doubt in this matter? They would say: No. He would then kill (the man) and then bring him back to life. When he would bring that person to life, he would say: By Allah, I had no better proof of the fact (that you are a Dajjal) than at the present time (that you are actually so). The Dajjal would then make an attempt to kill him (again) but he would not be able to do that. Abu Ishaq reported that it was said: That person would be Khadir (Allah be pleased with him). (Using translation from Muslim 2938a)"
"6802","What will be your state when the son of Mary descends amongst you and there will be an Imam amongst you? (Using translation from Muslim 155d)"
"6803","There will be no land which would not be covered by the Dajjal but Mecca and Medina, and there would no passage out of the passages leading to them which would not be guarded by angels arranged in rows. Then he (the Dajjal) would appear in a barren place adjacent to Medina and it would rock three times that every unbeliever and hypocrite would get out of it towards him. (Using translation from Muslim 2943a)"
"6804","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When Dajjal comes near Madinah, he will find angels: they will be guarding it, so Dajjal will not be able to enter Madinah, nor will the plague be able to enter it, if Allah wills."
"6805","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The terror caused by Al-Masih Ad-Dajjal will not enter Medina and at that time Medina will have seven gates and there will be two angels at each gate guarding them."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1879)"
"6806","The Jews will fight against you and you will gain victory over them until the stone would say: Muslim, here is a Jew behind me; kill him. (Using translation from Muslim 2921d)"
"6807","narrates: We were present with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned Dajjal and said: Your (mutual discord) is more frightening to me than the trial of Dajjal. Every small and big trial will be a precursor to the trial of Dajjal. Whoever is saved from the trials before it will also be saved from it, and it will not harm any Muslim, because between his two eyes, in letters, ""K F R"" (i.e., disbeliever) will be written."
"6808","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Ever since I heard three things from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), I have always loved Banu Tamim. Once, some of their people were brought as captives to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Among them was a captive who belonged to the descendants of Isma'il. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Set free the one who is from the descendants of Sayyiduna Isma'il (peace"
"6809","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""You will fight against the people of the Arabian Peninsula and Allah Almighty will grant you victory over them. You will fight against the people of Persia and Allah Almighty will grant you victory over them. Then you will fight against the Dajjal and Allah Almighty will grant you victory over him."
"6810","The Dajjal will come from the east, and his intention will be towards Madinah Munawwarah. When he camps near the mountain of Uhud, then he will set out towards Shaam, and there he will meet his destruction."
"6811","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Sayyiduna ‘Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) will kill the Dajjal near the gate of Ludd.”"
"6812","The Dajjal, who will bring misguidance, will appear from the east at a time of people's discord, and within forty days, as much as Allah wills, he will reach that part of the earth. Allah knows best about its extent. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this twice. Then Allah, the Exalted, will send down Sayyiduna Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him); he will lead those people (i.e., the Muslims) in prayer. When he raises his head from bowing, he will say: Allah has heard the praise of the one who praised Him. Then Allah, the Exalted, will have the Dajjal killed and will grant dominance to the believers. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, it is mentioned that he will lead them in prayer. By this, it is meant: he will order them to lead the prayer, because sometimes the Arabs attribute the action to the one who gives the command, just as they attribute it to the one who performs the action, as we have mentioned in other places in our books."
"6813","The Last Hour would not come until the Romans would land at al-A'maq or in Dabiq. An army consisting of the best (soldiers) of the people of the earth at that time will come from Medina (to counteract them). When they will arrange themselves in ranks, the Romans would say: Do not stand between us and those (Muslims) who took prisoners from amongst us. Let us fight with them; and the Muslims would say: Nay, by Allah, we would never get aside from you and from our brethren that you may fight them. They will then fight and a third (part) of the army would run away, whom Allah will never forgive. A third (part of the army) which would be constituted of excellent martyrs in Allah's eye, would be killed and the third who would never be put to trial would win and they would be conquerors of Constantinople. And as they would be busy in distributing the spoils of war (amongst themselves) after hanging their swords by the olive trees, the Satan would cry: The Dajjal has taken your place among your family. They would then come out, but it would be of no avail. And when they would come to Syria, he would come out while they would be still preparing themselves for battle drawing up the ranks. Certainly, the time of prayer shall come and then Jesus (peace be upon him) son of Mary would descend and would lead them. When the enemy of Allah would see him, it would (disappear) just as the salt dissolves itself in water and if he (Jesus) were not to confront them at all, even then it would dissolve completely, but Allah would kill them by his hand and he would show them their blood on his lance (the lance of Jesus Christ). (Using translation from Muslim 2897)"
"6814","I am the closest to ‘Isa ibn Maryam. When he descends, you will recognize him: he will be a man whose complexion is reddish-white, and it will appear as if drops of water are falling from his head, although his head will not be wet. He will break the cross, kill the swine, make wealth abundant, and abolish the jizya. Allah, the Exalted, will abolish every religion except Islam during his time, and Allah will destroy the misguided, one-eyed, lying Dajjal as well. Then Allah will instill peace and tranquility, so much so that the lion will graze with the camel, the leopard with the cow, and the wolf with the sheep; children will play with snakes, and none of them will harm another."
"6815","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Sayyiduna 'Isa ibn Maryam will come to a people whom Allah Almighty has protected from the Dajjal, so he will touch their faces according to their ranks in Paradise."
"6816","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Isa ibn Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary) will descend as a just and fair ruler. He will break the cross, kill the swine, abolish the jizya (tax), and camels will be left (no effort will be made to collect their zakat). Mutual hatred, malice, and envy will disappear. He will invite people to wealth, but no one will accept it."
"6817","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding the statement of Allah Almighty: ""Indeed, it is a sign of the Hour."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This refers to the descent of Sayyiduna Isa bin Maryam before the Day of Judgment."
"6818","""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Ibn Mariam shall soon descend among you, judging justly. He shall break the cross, kill the pig, remove the Jizyah, and wealth will be so bountiful that there will be none to accept it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2233)"
"6819","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A section of my people will not cease fighting for the Truth and will prevail till the Day of Resurrection. He said: Jesus son of Mary would then descend and their (Muslims') commander would invite him to come and lead them in prayer, but he would say: No, some amongst you are commanders over some (amongst you). This is the honour from Allah for this Ummah. (Using translation from Muslim 156)"
"6820","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""At the place of Faj Ruhā’, Sayyiduna ‘Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) will recite the talbiyah for Hajj, or perhaps for ‘Umrah, or perhaps for both (the narrator is unsure)."
"6821","I am the closest to ‘Isa ibn Maryam, because there is no Prophet between me and him. He will descend, and when you see him, you will recognize him: he is a man of reddish-white complexion, of medium height, and it will seem as if drops of water are falling from his head, though it will not be wet. He will fight the people for Islam, he will break the cross, kill the swine, and abolish the jizya. Allah, the Exalted, will destroy all religions except Islam during his time, and He will destroy the Masih al-Dajjal. Peace will be established on the earth, so much so that lions will graze with camels, leopards with cows, wolves with sheep, and children will play with snakes, and they will not harm them. Sayyiduna ‘Isa (peace be upon him) will remain on the earth for forty years, then he will pass away, and the Muslims will perform his funeral prayer. May Allah's blessings descend upon him."
"6822","Sayyiduna Isa ibn Maryam will descend, and he will kill him. Then Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) will remain on the earth for forty years (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) or close to forty years. He will remain as a just ruler, a ruler who judges with justice."
"6823","The Hour will not be established until the earth is filled with oppression and enmity. Then a man from my Ahl al-Bayt (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps the words are: from my progeny) will emerge who will fill the earth with justice and fairness, just as it was previously filled with oppression."
"6824","The Hour will not be established until a man from my Ahl al-Bayt becomes the ruler of the people. His name will be the same as my name, and his father's name will be the same as my father's name. He will fill the earth with justice and fairness."
"6825","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man will emerge from my Ummah whose name will be like my name, and his character will be like my character. He will fill the earth with justice and fairness just as it was previously filled with oppression and tyranny."
"6826","The Hour will not be established until a man from my Ahl al-Bayt becomes a ruler; he will fill the earth with justice just as it was filled with oppression before him. He will rule for seven years."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Sadiq is Bakr bin Qais Naji."
"6827","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioning from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Nob"
"6828","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Indeed, among Yajuj and Majuj, the least of them will be the one from whose back a thousand offspring will come, and after them three groups will appear: Mansak, Taweel, and Tarees. Only Allah Almighty knows their number.”"
"6829","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: So the people, out of fear of them, will flee towards their forts."
"6830","The Muslims will say, 'Is there anyone who will risk his life for us and find out what has happened to this enemy?' So one person among them will separate himself for this task, preparing himself for the possibility of being killed. Then he will find that they are all dead, lying one upon another. He will call out: 'O group of Muslims! Rejoice! Glad tidings to you! Allah Almighty has sufficed you against your enemy.' So the people will come out of their cities and fortresses and will release their livestock."
"6831","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up red in the face and said: ‘La ilaha illallah, woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn nigh. Today a hole has been opened in the barrier of Gog and Magog.’ And he gestured to indicate the size of the hole.” Zainab said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! Will we be destroyed when there are righteous people among us?’ He said: ‘If sin and evil deeds increase.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3953)"
"6832","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even after the emergence of Gog and Magog, Hajj and 'Umrah to this House of Allah will still be performed."
"6833","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(Before the Day of Judgment) some signs will appear, and they will come one after another in such a way that (when a necklace breaks) its beads fall one after another.”"
"6834","I heard my father quoting the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) as saying: ""A group from my Ummah will always be helped; whoever tries to disgrace them will not harm them in any way, until the Day of Resurrection is established."
"6835","The opposition of those who oppose them will not harm them in any way, until Allah's command comes to them and they will be in this state."
"6836","I was in the company of Maslama b. Mukhallad, and 'Abdullah b. 'Amr b. 'As was with him. 'Abdullah said: The Hour shall some oniy when the worst type of people are left on the earth. They will be worse than the people of pre-Islamic days. They will get whatever they ask of Allah. While we were yet sitting when 'Uqba b. 'Amir came, and Maslama said to him: 'Uqba, listen to what 'Abdullah says. 'Uqba said: He knows better; so far as I am concerned, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A group of people from my Umma will continue to fight in obedience to the Command of Allah, remaining dominant over their enemies. Those who will oppose them shall not do them any harm. They will remain ill this condition until the Hour overtakes them. (At this) 'Abdullah said: Yes. Then Allah will raise a wild which will be fragrant like musk and whose touch will be like the touch of silk; (but) it will cause the death of all (faithful) persons, not leaving behind a single person with an iota of faith in his heart. Then only the worst of men will remain to be overwhelmed by the Hour. (Using translation from Muslim 1924)"
"6837","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of Muslims will always continue to fight for this religion until the Day of Resurrection is established."
"6838","The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from the west. When it rises from the west, all people will believe, but on that day, the faith of no person will benefit him who did not believe before, or who did not earn any good through his faith."
"6839","The Hour will not be established until a fire appears which will illuminate the necks of the camels in Busra."
"6840","The fire has set out, so O people, you also set out. The fire is resting, so O people, you also rest. The fire has departed, so O people, you also depart. The fire will consume whoever it reaches."
"6841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did they hasten towards Madinah and the women? If they had left those women as they were (i.e., had not gone early last night), it would have been better. However, the people who stayed behind with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he spoke to them appropriately. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Alas! When a fire will emerge from the mountain of Waraq in Yemen, it will illuminate the necks of the camels, and that fire will descend upon Busra just as daylight descends."" The narrator named Ali bin Madini says: The place called Busra is in Syria."
"6842","""The hour shall not be established until time is constricted, and the year is like a month, a month is like the week, and the week is like the day, and the day is like the hour, and the hour is like the flare of the fire."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2332)"
"6843","Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us all of a sudden as we were (busy in a discussion). He said: What do you discuss about? They (the Companions) said. We are discussing about the Last Hour. Thereupon he said: It will not come until you see ten signs before and (in this connection) he made a mention of the smoke, Dajjal, the beast, the rising of the sun from the west, the descent of Jesus son of Mary (Allah be pleased with him), the Gog and Magog, and land-slides in three places, one in the east, one in the west and one in Arabia at the end of which fire would burn forth from the Yemen, and would drive people to the place of their assembly. (Using translation from Muslim 2901a)"
"6844","The trustworthy person will be considered treacherous, and the treacherous person will be made trustworthy. The 'Da'ul' will be destroyed and 'Tahut' will become common."" The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by 'Da'ul' and 'Tahut'?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Da'ul' refers to the elders and respected people among the people, and 'Tahut' refers to those people who remain under the feet of the people and are not known about."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sa'id bin Jubair heard ahadith from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) at a time when he was ten years old."
"6845","The Hour will certainly be established while (two men’s) cloth is between them, but they will neither be able to wrap it nor finalize its sale. The Hour will certainly be established while a man is returning with his she-camel’s milk, but he will not be able to drink it. The Hour will certainly be established while a person is repairing his pond, but he will not be able to drink from it. The Hour will certainly be established while a man raises a morsel to his mouth, but he will not be able to eat it."
"6846","The Hour will be established upon people while there will be a cloth between them, about which they will be concluding a deal, but they will neither be able to spread it nor fold it. The Hour will be established upon a person while there will be a morsel in his mouth, but he will neither be able to swallow it nor spit it out."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Harith is Muhammad bin Ziyad, and the narrator named Maisur is the son of Abdur Rahman."
"6847","The worst among the people will be those whom the Hour (Day of Judgment) finds alive, and (among the worst of people are) those who make graves places of prostration."
"6848","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The Hour will not be established upon anyone who says La ilaha illallah.\"""""""
"6849","""The Hour (Resurrection) will not occur until 'Allah, Allah' is not said on earth."" (Using translation from Muslim 148a)"
"6850","The Last Hour would affect (most terribly) the wicked persons. (Using translation from Muslim 2949)"
"6851","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Soon you will be selected just as a date is picked out from its (husks and the like)."
"6852","The righteous people will be taken (from the world) as predecessors, and the righteous will perish one by one, until only such people will remain who will be like the useless and worthless husks of dates. Allah Almighty will not care about them."
"6853","The Hour will not be established until a red wind blows from Yemen, and through this wind Allah, the Exalted, will seize the soul of every person who believes in Allah and the Last Day. Due to the small number of people dying in it, people will not consider it strange (and will say), 'The old man of such-and-such tribe died in it, and the old woman of such-and-such tribe died in it.' The Book of Allah will be separated and raised up towards the sky; not a single verse of it will remain on the earth. The earth will vomit out its treasures, that is, gold and silver, but after that day, no one will be able to benefit from them. A person will pass by them, strike them with his foot, and say: 'Did the people before us use to fight each other because of these? Today, it is such that no benefit can be taken from them.'"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""Among the Arab tribes, the first to perish will be the Quraysh. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, soon a time will come when a person will pass by a shoe lying on a garbage heap, he will pick it up with his hand and then say, 'Shoes like this used to belong to the Quraysh.'"
"6854","The people said: O Messenger of Allah! This means knowledge, which Allah Almighty granted you, until when you were filled with it and some remained, you gave it to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have spoken the truth."
"6855",""" Messenger of Allah ﷺ is reported to have said: Behold I am free from the dependence of all bosom friends and if I were to choose anyone as bosom friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as my bosom friend. Allah has taken your companion as a friend. (Using translation from Muslim 2383e)"
"6856","If I were to choose a bosom friend I would have definitely chosen Abu Bakr as my bosom friend, but he is my brother and my companion and Allah, the Exalted and Gliorious. has taken your brother and companion (meaning Prophet himself) as a friend. (Using translation from Muslim 2383a)"
"6857","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that all the doors of the mosque opening towards the pathway be closed, except for the specific door of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6858","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The wealth of none of you has benefited me as much as the wealth of Abu Bakr.'"" Abu Bakr wept and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I and my wealth are only for you, O Messenger of Allah.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 94)"
"6859","narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) spent forty thousand (dirhams or dinars) on the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6860","I were to take anyone from among the people as a close friend (khalil), I would have taken Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam remains. Close all the doors in the mosque except the specific door for Abu Bakr (to enter). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), ""Close all the doors in the mosque except Abu Bakr's door,"" contains evidence that after the Prophet (peace be upon him), the caliph of the Muslims would be Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), because the Prophet (peace be upon him) knew that among all the people, they might desire to be the caliph after him, except for Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), about whom he knew that he would not desire this. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Close every door for entering the mosque except the specific door for Abu Bakr (do not close it)."
"6861","that Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the pulpit and said, ""Allah gave a choice to a servant that he may opt for the beauties of the world or that which is with Him. And the servant chose that which was with Him."" Thereupon Abū Bakr wept and he wept a lot and said: ""Let our fathers and our mothers be taken as ransom for you."" It was Messenger of Allah ﷺ who had been given the choice, and Abū Bakr knew it better than us."",""Messenger of Allah ﷺ is reported to have said"",""""""Behold"","" of all people the most generous toward me in regard to his companionship and his property was Abū Bakr. Were I to choose anyone as my khalīl (close friend)"","" I would have chosen Abū Bakr as my khalīl"","" but ˹for him I cherish˺ Islamic brotherhood. There shall be left open no window ˹facing˺ Masjid ˹al-Nabawī˺ except Abū Bakr's window."""" (Using translation from Muslim 2382a)"""""
"6862","""Abu Bakr is our chief, and the best of us, and the most beloved of us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3656)"
"6863","that Abu Bakr said: ""Am I not the most deserving of it among the people, am I not the first to become Muslim, am I not the person of such and such, am I not the person of such and such."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3667)"
"6864","The name of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was Abdullah bin Uthman. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""You are a person freed from Hell by Allah Almighty."" Because of this, he was named Atiq (i.e., the freed one)."
"6865","The prophet of Allah ﷺ ascended Uhud, and Abu Bakr, ’Umar and 'Uthman followed him. It began to shake with them. The prophet of Allah ﷺ struck it with his foot and said: Be still, for only a prophet, an ever-truthful and two martyrs are on you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4651)"
"6866","""Whoever spends on a pair (of things) in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, he will be called in Paradise: 'O slave of Allah, here is prosperity, Whoever is one of the people of Salah, he will be called from the gate of salah. Whoever is on of the people of charity, he will be called from the gate of Ar-Rayyan.' Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said: 'O Messenger of Allah, no distress or need will befall the one who is called from those gates. Will there be anyone who will be called from all these gates?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2238)"
"6867","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Yes, O Abu Bakr, that will be you.'"
"6868","The women and children of the polytheists would come and stand by him and be amazed at him; they would keep looking at him, because Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was a man who wept much. When he recited the Qur'an, his tears would not stop. This frightened the nobles of Quraysh. They sent a message to Ibn Daghina, who came to them, and they said: We granted Abu Bakr protection because of you on the condition that he would worship Allah in his house. He has violated this and built a mosque in his courtyard, and prays and recites openly. We fear that he may put our women and children to trial. If he is content to worship his Lord inside his house, that is fine; but if he does not accept and continues to do so openly, then you must tell him to return your protection, for we do not like to violate your protection, nor can we allow Abu Bakr to do this openly. Ibn Daghina came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: O Abu Bakr, you know on what condition I granted you protection. Either you be content with that, or return my protection to me, for I do not like that the Arabs should hear that I withdrew protection from someone after granting it. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I return your protection to you and am content with the protection of Allah and His Messenger. (Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates) The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was residing in Makkah in those days. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to the Muslims: The land of your migration has been shown to me (in a dream). I saw that it is a land of date palms, between two rocky tracts. (Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates) When the Prophet (peace be upon him) mentioned this, those who had to migrate left for Madinah, and some of those Muslims who had previously migrated to Abyssinia also came to Madinah. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also prepared for migration, but the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: Wait, for I hope that I too will be granted permission (to migrate). Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: Do you hope for that, may my parents be sacrificed for you? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: Yes. So Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) held himself back for the Prophet (peace be upon him). He fed his camels with acacia leaves for four months. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once, we were sitting in our house at noon, when someone said to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace be upon him) has arrived. The Prophet (peace be upon him) had covered his face, and it was an hour in which he would not usually come to us. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: May my parents be sacrificed for him, he must have come for some important matter. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) came and sought permission to enter, then entered. When he came in, he said to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): Remove those around you from the house. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, these are only your family (no one else is here). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I have been given permission to depart. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, I will accompany you. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Yes. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, take one of these two she-camels. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I will take it for a price. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then we prepared provisions for both of them and put them in a leather bag. Lady Asma bint Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) tore her waistband and tied the mouth of the bag with it, and for this she was called ""Dhat an-Nitaqayn"" (the one with the two waistbands). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the cave in the mountain called Thawr, where they stayed for three days."
"6869","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think about two people with whom the third is Allah, the Exalted?"
"6870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down. I looked around to see if any of the pursuers could be seen, and there I saw a shepherd bringing his sheep towards the rock. He too wanted to get from the rock what I wanted, i.e., shade. I asked him: O boy! Whose slave are you? The boy said: So-and-so. He mentioned the name of a man from the Quraysh whom I knew. I asked: Do your sheep have milk? He replied: Yes. I asked: Will you milk one for us? He said: Yes. I instructed him, and he separated one sheep from the flock. I told him to clean the dust from it, and then I told him to dust off his hands as well. So he did so, striking one hand against the other. Then he milked the sheep into a vessel. I had a vessel with me for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), with a cloth over its mouth. I poured water over the milk until the lower part became cool (i.e., the water mixed well with the milk). Then I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I found him awake. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Please drink this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) drank it. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Now it is time to depart. So we set out, and people were searching for us, but none of them reached us except Suraqah bin Malik, who reached us on his horse. I said: O Messenger of Allah! The pursuer has reached us. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I began to weep, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not fear. Indeed, Allah is with us. When he came close and there was only the distance of two or three spears between us and him, I said: O Messenger of Allah! The pursuer has reached us. I began to weep at this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Why are you weeping? I said: By Allah! I am not weeping for myself, but I am weeping for your sake. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed against that man. He said: O Allah! Be sufficient for us against him as You will. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The horse of that man sank into the ground up to its belly, and he fell off it. Then he said: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), I know that this has happened because of your action. Pray to Allah for me to be saved from this situation. By Allah! I will mislead those who come after me searching for you. Here is my quiver; take an arrow from it. When you pass by my camels and sheep at such-and-such a place, take from them whatever you need. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: We have no need of your camels. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for him, and he returned to his companions. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) continued traveling until we reached Madinah at night. There was disagreement among the people as to where the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would stay. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Tonight I will stay with Banu Najjar, who are the maternal relatives of ‘Abdul Muttalib. I will honor them in this regard. When we arrived in Madinah, people came out into the streets, children were on the rooftops, and slaves were present. They were saying: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has arrived! The Messenger of Allah has arrived! When morning came, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) set out and camped at the place where he was commanded to do so. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray facing Bayt al-Maqdis for about sixteen or seventeen months. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wished that his direction be changed towards the Ka‘bah, so Allah revealed this verse: “We have certainly seen the turning of your face, [O Muhammad], toward the heaven, and We will surely turn you to a qiblah with which you will be pleased. So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram.” The narrator says: Some foolish people among the Jews said: “What has turned them away from their qiblah which they used to face?” So Allah revealed this verse: “Say: To Allah belong the east and the west. He guides whom He wills to a straight path.” The narrator states: A man prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and after praying, he left and passed by some Ansar who were in the bowing position during the ‘Asr prayer, facing Bayt al-Maqdis. He informed them that he bore witness that he had prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had turned his face towards the Ka‘bah. So they turned around and faced the Ka‘bah. Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The first of the Muhajirun to come to us was Sayyiduna Mus‘ab bin ‘Umayr (may Allah be pleased with him), who belonged to Banu ‘Abd al-Dar bin Qays. We asked him: How is the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? He replied: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is in his place, and some of his companions are coming after me. Then after him, Sayyiduna ‘Amr bin Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him), who was blind and belonged to Banu Fihr, came to us. We asked him: After you, how is the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions? He replied: They are coming after me. Then after them, Sayyiduna ‘Ammar bin Yasir, Sayyiduna Sa‘d bin Abi Waqqas, Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah bin Mas‘ud, and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them) came to us. Then Sayyiduna ‘Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us with some riders. Then after them, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us, and with him was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us, I had already learned to recite twenty surahs from the mufassal surahs. Then we set out to intercept (Abu Sufyan’s) caravan, but we found that they had already escaped (i.e., this refers to the occasion of the Battle of Badr)."
"6871","I come again and do not find you? The woman meant, if you have passed away, then what should I do? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr."
"6872","The woman meant, if you have passed away (then what should I do)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr."
"6873","""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became seriously ill, Bilal came to tell him it was time to pray and he said: 'Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.""' She said: ""I said: '0 Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and when he stands in your place he will not be able to make the people hear his voice; why don't you tell 'Umar (to do it)?' He said: 'Tell a Abu Bakr to lead the people in the prayer.' I said to Hafsah: 'Tell him.' So she told him. He said: 'You are (like) the female companions of Yosuf. Tell Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.""' She said: ""So they told Abu Bakr. When he started to pray, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to feel better, so he got up and came with the help of two men, with his feet dragging along the ground. (When) he entered the Masjid, Abu Bakr heard him coming and he wanted to step back, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him: 'Stay where you are.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and sat on Abu Bakr's left, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leading the people in prayer sitting, and Abu Bakr was standing and following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people were following the prayer of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 833)"
"6874","I repeated this matter before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I repeated it because I feared that people would feel uneasy with regard to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), because I knew that whoever stood in the place of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), people would take it as a bad omen (uneasiness), so I wished that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would remove Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) from this matter."
"6875","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When Monday came, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted the curtain of his chamber. He (peace be upon him) saw Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), who was leading the people in prayer. The narrator says: I looked at the face of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and it was as bright as a page of the Qur'an. He (peace be upon him) was smiling. It was so close that, out of the joy of seeing th"
"6876","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Once the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was delivering a sermon when a caravan (that is, a caravan of goods) arrived in Madinah Munawwarah. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) hurried towards it until only twelve people remained, among whom were Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). At that time, this verse was reveal"
